# Top-level H5000M plugin packages baked into the OPTIONAL "loaded" image.
# The clean official base never contains these - it is built and asserted first, and the
# forbidden-package check guarantees they did not leak into it. This list applies only to
# the second artifact produced when H5000M_LOADED_IMAGE=1.
#
# Only top-level packages belong here. Their dependencies (the AT broker, and the in-feed
# packages such as kmod-usb-serial-option, kmod-usb-net-rndis, 464xlat, kmod-nat46, lpac,
# travelmate, tailscale, mwan3 and the LuCI apps) are resolved by apk from the signed
# plugin repo plus the official feeds.
h5000m-fm350
# Must be listed explicitly: luci-proto-fm350 DEPENDS on h5000m-fm350, not the reverse, so
# nothing pulls it in. Without it LuCI renders the cellular interface as "unsupported
# protocol type" and offers no form at all - verified missing from the r35551 loaded image.
luci-proto-fm350
# Network -> FM350: status, SMS and recovery. Like luci-proto-fm350 nothing depends on it,
# so it must be listed explicitly or it never lands in the image.
luci-app-fm350
h5000m-lpac
# SMS over the modem's single AT port, via sms_tool run under at-lease. sms_tool itself
# comes from the official feed and handles PDU/UCS2/multipart, so this ships no codec.
h5000m-sms
h5000m-travelmate-defaults
h5000m-tailscale-defaults
h5000m-mwan3-policy
# TTL/hop-limit normaliser for the cellular uplink. Off by default (enabled='0'), so shipping
# it costs nothing until it is switched on. Listed explicitly because nothing depends on it -
# the same reason luci-proto-fm350 and luci-app-fm350 are here.
h5000m-ttl
# Router-side FIFO archive for SMS: watches the modem's ~90-slot store and moves the
# oldest messages to /etc/h5000m/sms-archive.json before it fills and starts rejecting
# new ones SILENTLY. Ships enabled='0', so it costs nothing until switched on. Listed
# explicitly because nothing depends on it.
h5000m-sms-archive

# --- v2rayA proxy manager (2026-07-28) --------------------------------------------------
# Unlike everything above, these are NOT signed h5000m-* wrappers: v2rayA and its whole
# stack already live in the official feeds, so they are baked straight in - no source build
# and no plugin repo (contrast PassWall2, third-party and still deferred). They ship with
# upstream package defaults: v2rayA runs its own web UI on tcp/2017 (LAN-only behind the
# default firewall), with no baked nodes or routing and a first-run admin setup in the
# browser. Every name here is asserted present by the loaded-image manifest check.
v2raya
# LuCI menu entry that links to the v2rayA UI; depends on v2raya.
luci-app-v2raya
# Simplified-Chinese LuCI strings. VERIFIED the feed ships this as zh-cn, not zh-hans.
luci-i18n-v2raya-zh-cn
# Proxy engine. xray-core is the VLESS/XTLS/Reality superset of v2ray-core; v2rayA declares
# no hard core dependency, so the engine must be listed explicitly or none is installed.
xray-core
# Routing databases (geoip.dat/geosite.dat) the engine consults for rule-based and
# GFW-style routing. Listed explicitly - nothing pulls them in.
v2ray-geoip
v2ray-geosite
# Transparent-gateway proxy. kmod-nft-tproxy provides the nft `tproxy` statement; v2rayA's
# generated ruleset also uses the nft `socket` match, so kmod-nft-socket is its mandatory
# companion - tproxy without it means the transparent rules never load. Both are forbidden
# in the clean base (plugin-owned) and belong only here.
kmod-nft-tproxy
kmod-nft-socket
